From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Venus Build Fix <noreply@example.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] bcm2712_defconfig: disable the cpuset cgroup v1 legacy
 interface

raspberrypi5 uses its own bcm2712_defconfig, separate from
bcm2711_defconfig used by raspberrypi4-64 - the existing
0002-bcm2711-disable-cpusets-v1-legacy-interface.patch only touches
the latter, so raspberrypi5 never got the same fix despite sharing
this recipe. Apply the identical change here for consistency: v1 vs
v2 cgroup mounting is a runtime choice (cgroup_no_v1= boot param),
but CONFIG_CPUSETS_V1 is the compile-time toggle for the legacy-only
per-controller cpuset interface, and container workloads only need
the unified (v2) hierarchy.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [Venus specific]

---
 arch/arm64/configs/bcm2712_defconfig | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/arch/arm64/configs/bcm2712_defconfig
+++ b/arch/arm64/configs/bcm2712_defconfig
@@ -25,7 +25,7 @@
 CONFIG_CGROUP_PIDS=y
 CONFIG_CGROUP_FREEZER=y
 CONFIG_CPUSETS=y
-CONFIG_CPUSETS_V1=y
+# CONFIG_CPUSETS_V1 is not set
 CONFIG_CGROUP_DEVICE=y
 CONFIG_CGROUP_CPUACCT=y
 CONFIG_CGROUP_PERF=y
--
